---
import Shell from "../layouts/Shell.astro";
---
<Shell title="Terms of Use | Regidi Lab" section="terms" description="Conditions for using the Regidi Lab proof of concept">
  <div class="container content-page privacy-page" lang="en" dir="ltr">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">ROUNVER RESEARCH / TERMS</p>
      <h1>Terms <em>of use</em></h1>
      <p>Conditions for using the Regidi Lab proof of concept Last updated: November 22, 2026.</p>
    </header>
    <p class="privacy-intro">Regidi Lab is an open research and demonstration environment. Access is free, no registration is needed, and it does not support real-world transactions. These terms describe what the experience is for and its limitations.</p>
    <ol class="privacy-sections">
      <li id="alcance"><span class="mono privacy-number">01</span><div>
        <h2>Nature and scope of the service</h2>
        <p>Regidi Lab is an experimental proof of concept by Rounver Corp. exploring cryptographic identity, delegated permissions, and verification of AI agent requests. It is provided solely for informational, educational, technical, and research purposes.</p>
        <p>The lab simulates a fictional authorizer, an issuer, and receiving services representing an airline and a bank. It does not establish real human identities, verify anyone's legal authority to act, or execute real bookings, payments, or transfers.</p>
      </div></li>
      <li id="aceptacion"><span class="mono privacy-number">02</span><div>
        <h2>Access and acceptance</h2>
        <p>By using the lab, you accept these terms to the extent permitted under applicable law. If you do not agree, you may stop using it at any time.</p>
        <p>No account or personal information is required. Access is subject to platform availability and anti-abuse safeguards.</p>
      </div></li>
      <li id="uso-aceptable"><span class="mono privacy-number">03</span><div>
        <h2>Acceptable use and restrictions</h2>
        <p>You may explore the intended scenarios, inspect permissions, test denied requests, and analyze the public behavior of the demonstration.</p>
        <p>You must not disrupt the site, bypass security controls or rate limits, automate abusive requests, exploit vulnerabilities without authorization, access resources belonging to others, or enter actual personal data or credentials in test fields.</p>
        <p>Rounver Corp. may limit or suspend technical access when traffic threatens the lab's availability or security.</p>
      </div></li>
      <li id="sesiones-claves"><span class="mono privacy-number">04</span><div>
        <h2>Sessions, keys, and permissions</h2>
        <p>When a test agent is created, the browser generates a non-exportable private key and registers its public counterpart for the demonstration. The private key remains in the browser. The session starts with a five-minute lifetime and, when authorization is granted, expires with the selected three-, five-, or fifteen-minute permission.</p>
        <p>Permissions issued here are fictional, limited in scope and duration, and revocable within the lab. No test credential provides authority to act on third-party services.</p>
      </div></li>
      <li id="pagos"><span class="mono privacy-number">05</span><div>
        <h2>Free access, payments, and cancellation</h2>
        <p>Regidi Lab is offered free of charge. There are no subscriptions, invoices, balances, payment gateways, or charges for its simulated scenarios. Accordingly, no refund policy applies to the use of this demonstration.</p>
        <p>Visitors may leave the lab or restart their session at any time. Technical-record deletion is explained in the <a href='/privacy/'>Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
      </div></li>
      <li id="disponibilidad"><span class="mono privacy-number">06</span><div>
        <h2>Changes and experimental availability</h2>
        <p>The proof of concept may be changed, restarted, suspended, or withdrawn as research evolves. Results, examples, and behavior may vary between versions.</p>
        <p>No contractual commitments are provided for uptime, response time, continuity, technical support, or interoperability with independent systems.</p>
      </div></li>
      <li id="propiedad"><span class="mono privacy-number">07</span><div>
        <h2>Code, documentation, and intellectual property</h2>
        <p>Names, materials, text, design, and identifying elements of Regidi Lab and Rounver Research belong to their respective owners. Publicly available source code or documentation are governed by the specific licenses supplied with those materials.</p>
        <p>Use of the lab does not grant trademark rights or authorize presenting this demonstration as an official certification, approved standard, or verified-identity product.</p>
      </div></li>
      <li id="garantias"><span class="mono privacy-number">08</span><div>
        <h2>Disclaimer of warranties and liability</h2>
        <p>The lab is provided “as is” as an experimental environment. We do not warrant that it is production-ready, error-free, or suitable for actual legal, banking, or commercial decisions.</p>
        <p>To the extent permitted by law, Rounver Corp. is not responsible for decisions or losses arising from treating simulated results as valid verification or authorization for real-world operations. Nothing in these terms limits non-waivable statutory rights.</p>
      </div></li>
      <li id="legislacion"><span class="mono privacy-number">09</span><div>
        <h2>Applicable law and restrictions</h2>
        <p>Rounver Corp. is incorporated in Delaware, United States. These terms are interpreted under applicable law, without prejudice to mandatory user-protection rules where they apply.</p>
        <p>Access and use must comply with applicable trade, export, and sanctions laws and restrictions in the relevant jurisdiction. We do not represent that access is unrestricted in every territory.</p>
      </div></li>
      <li id="contacto"><span class="mono privacy-number">10</span><div>
        <h2>Updates and contact</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms when making significant changes to the lab. The current revision date is shown at the top of this page.</p>
        <p>For legal inquiries related to Regidi Lab, email <a href='mailto:privacy@rounver.com'>privacy@rounver.com</a>. You may also read the <a href='/privacy/'>Privacy Policy</a> and the <a href='/security/'>Security Policy</a>.</p>
      </div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</Shell>
